From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 10:33:30 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 207/342] kernel/vm: the page writer writes a small queue after
 its idle wait

Since the per-device page writers (3bfaa91290), a timed-out wait went
back to waiting, so fewer than 256 modified pages were only written by
a sync, a quota or an unmount. Data written minutes before a power loss
was lost, while BFS's journal kept the inodes pointing at blocks that
held whatever was there before (found on a C2's eMMC: test programs
holding pages of deleted package uploads). Write the queue after each
idle wait again, as before the rewrite.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/system/kernel/vm/vm_page_writer.cpp | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/system/kernel/vm/vm_page_writer.cpp b/src/system/kernel/vm/vm_page_writer.cpp
index 82116500dc..c15e0c0f4c 100644
--- a/src/system/kernel/vm/vm_page_writer.cpp
+++ b/src/system/kernel/vm/vm_page_writer.cpp
@@ -565,9 +565,12 @@ ModifiedPageQueue::_PageWriter()
 
 	while (fWriterThread >= 0) {
 		if (queue.Count() < kNumPages) {
-			// wait the full amount when no one triggers us
-			if (!fPageWriterCondition.Wait(PAGES_FLUSH_DURATION_LOCAL_QUOTA, true))
-				continue;
+			// Wait the full amount when no one triggers us, then write what
+			// is queued anyway: otherwise fewer than kNumPages modified pages
+			// stay in memory until a sync, and a power loss loses data that
+			// was written long before it (while the journal kept the
+			// metadata pointing at blocks that were never written).
+			fPageWriterCondition.Wait(PAGES_FLUSH_DURATION_LOCAL_QUOTA, true);
 		}
 
 		page_num_t modifiedPages = queue.Count();
